  "claims": [
    "A new catalogue embeds every old completed MAC/structural rule and adds suffix sequential-wire fusion: wire(p);(wire(q);T) rewrites to wire(p;q);T. Its symbolic charges are balanced and its support is exactly T.needs.",
    "Every new primitive, contextual step and reversible proof track expands into an old proof track, preserving its exact finite guard support. Old primitive/step/track/path embeddings preserve supports, and expanding an embedded old step or track yields that same old syntax.",
    "Any old checked model extends to the new catalogue with the same base kernels. macModel instantiates this extension with the existing full-state/trace MAC model and unchanged indexed conditions.",
    "The new higher presentation imports explicit old context-generated local generators, not whole arbitrary old higher cells, and adds one suffix-fusion definition schema plus contextual closure. An old higher cell is translated recursively with unchanged support and Four-constructor count.",
    "eliminateTrack constructs, for every new proof track P, a higher comparison between P and the embedding of its old expansion. The comparison support equals P.support, including under composition, formal inverse, and all four mixed placements.",
    "projectCell maps every new higher cell to a comparison of its expanded old boundaries with exactly the same support. liftCoherence reconstructs a new comparison from an explicitly supplied comparison of the expanded old boundaries, with support exactly equal to that supplied old comparison.",
    "comparison_iff proves that two new tracks admit a comparison exactly when their old expansions admit one. This is relative comparability, not a global coherence assumption or a claimed inverse pair on higher-cell syntax.",
    "Fresh repair support is unchanged when lifting an old comparison. The repaired joint-kernel theorem retains arbitrary correlated prior data and original input, using only an updated checked old model, cached guards, transfer outside the changed set and rechecked changed guards.",
    "The general association/wire-fusion peak has an actual higher cell derived from the definition schema and proof-groupoid laws; its support is T.needs and its Four-constructor count is twelve.",
    "The previously proved old-catalogue nonconfluent pair now has a joining path in the new catalogue: zero steps from the direct endpoint and two from the associated endpoint. For every stage n the joining path uses exactly guard {n+1}. Copy and discard placements preserve that support."
  ],
